{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"A host firewall is enabled on node1 and remains enabled with the intended policy after restart.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The configured firewall was healthy before reboot, the scheduled reboot produced an observable interruption and a new boot ID, and firewalld, sshd, interface assignment, runtime policy, permanent policy, and enforcement all recovered afterward. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1a616ac338924a3f","cmd-e73fb3d60a5f4527","cmd-07367a31d10c4ba0","cmd-91791eefe5a544d4","cmd-12e50e41ba794fe8","cmd-9ad5e213270646cc","cmd-812ff352f60345a4","cmd-edbbed16cc9c45dd","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Inbound SSH and TCP port 8080 are permitted.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A post-restart ingress test against node1's managed IPv4 address showed an OpenSSH banner on TCP/22 and HTTP 200 on TCP/8080. The live nftables allow chain contains both ports.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5397d9f2beb14404","cmd-edbbed16cc9c45dd","cmd-4eff0bdd91e4451e","cmd-d9b2f95e17084bfb"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Unrelated inbound connections are rejected.","status":"satisfied","summary":"TCP/9090 was demonstrably listening yet an inbound connection to node1's managed address was immediately rejected. The nftables input path dispatches enp1s0 through the public zone and terminates unmatched input with reject rules.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5397d9f2beb14404","cmd-edbbed16cc9c45dd","cmd-18eee980c9504da8","cmd-d9b2f95e17084bfb"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The retained firewalld and NetworkManager changes directly implement the requested policy. Three bounded namespace/veth/listener setups supplied pre-restart, recovered-state, and managed-address behavior evidence and were each removed. The reboot served both persistence verification and the mandatory restart protocol. Final observations show no failed services, damaged package state, new listener exposure, or abandoned test artifacts; temporary-file differences are normal reboot-generated systemd-private directories.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7ef307a9c63845ff","cmd-962b94c0dfc140f1","cmd-20c1fb888e154986","cmd-025e570eec6442fc","cmd-07367a31d10c4ba0","cmd-9483511a60244358","cmd-31337427cdf44202","cmd-5397d9f2beb14404","cmd-80483b904ed74b1b","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory restart protocol is complete for the sole managed node: it captures healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement and interruption, a different boot identity independently cross-checked by lifecycle observations, and recovered services, configuration, listeners, and firewall behavior. No separate application-data or multi-node cluster state was applicable.","limitations":["Functional ingress was generated from an isolated local namespace/veth rather than an independent off-node source; direct nftables evidence mapping enp1s0 to the same public policy substantially mitigates this limitation (cmd-5397d9f2beb14404, cmd-d9b2f95e17084bfb).","TCP/9090 was the sole behaviorally sampled unrelated port; rejection of other unmatched inbound traffic is supported by the observed terminal nftables reject path (cmd-edbbed16cc9c45dd, cmd-18eee980c9504da8, cmd-d9b2f95e17084bfb)."]}
